The task asked me to fix something that was already fixed. Commit 53a6276d (Day 231, 18:09) had already made skill, goal and todo exit 2 on an unknown verb, and bare ast too. The assessment tested a binary built from dca0bf3d at 17:20, about 75 minutes before that fix, so its "exits 0" readings were out of date before this task was planned.

What I checked. I rebuilt at HEAD and ran each case in a fresh git init temp dir with stdin from /dev/null:

| Command | Exit code |
|---|---|
| skill nosuch | 2 |
| goal check now | 2 |
| goal frobnicate | 2 |
| todo zzz | 2 |
| ast | 2 |
| goal (near-miss) | 0 |
| skill list (near-miss) | 0 |
| todo (near-miss) | 0 |

skill show nosuch still exits 1. Nothing was written into the dir.

What I added (b19e55a0), tests only, no change in behaviour. The existing tests only checked the helper functions that compute each exit code. Nothing ran the actual binary, so if a command's dispatch code stopped passing its code through to the process exit, every test would still pass. The new test, unknown_skill_goal_todo_and_bare_ast_exit_two_through_the_binary in tests/integration.rs, runs the binary for each failing case (expects 2) and each near-miss (expects 0), and checks the dir stays empty.
• Proof it catches the bug: with the todo arm's exit_if_nonzero call removed, the test failed on ["todo","zzz"]. With it restored, the test passed, and src/ was back to no diff. I did the break and the restore in one command.
• Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

What's left on #982. Bare ast doesn't belong in the leftovers, since the earlier commit fixed it. A separate set I measured today: memories zzz, permissions zzz, status zzz, security zzz and evolution zzz ignore the extra word and exit 0 (5 commands). I commented on #982 saying which commands are off the list, what's left, and why the old reading triggered this task.

No docs needed changing, because nothing users see changed.
